            <ArticleTitle>Usefulness of the lymphocyte concentration as a prognostic marker in coronary artery disease.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>812-4</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>The prognostic utility of the relative lymphocyte concentration was tested in a population-based study of chronic coronary artery disease. This inexpensive, readily available test was found to be significantly related to survival (p = 0.03) in 211 patients followed for a mean of 45 months.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
